.TH tapectl-collection-run 1  "tapectl-collection-run " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-collection\-run \- Execute one batch: stage every unit in it once, write one session per destination label, then release staging. Targets a single collection (unlike `sync`/`status`/`plan`, which sweep every configured collection) since a batch write is a real, one\-shot tape action
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl collection run\fR <\fB\-\-collection\fR> [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-batch\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute one batch: stage every unit in it once, write one session per destination label, then release staging. Targets a single collection (unlike `sync`/`status`/`plan`, which sweep every configured collection) since a batch write is a real, one\-shot tape action
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-collection\fR \fI<COLLECTION>\fR
Collection name
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-batch\fR \fI<BATCH>\fR [default: 0]
Which batch from `collection plan`\*(Aqs ordering to execute (0 = first)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABELS>\fR
Destination volume label — already `volume init`\*(Aqd on its own cartridge. Repeat once per planned copy (e.g. `\-\-label L1 \-\-label L2` for two copies)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR [default: /dev/nst0]
Tape device path
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
